---- MODULE rendercontract ----
\* Generated by `spk compile` from spec `render.contract` — source of truth is the
\* spec file; edit there, not here. Extends nothing: the module is
\* self-contained so any engine can open it.

\* No executable invariant fragments (Revision 15).

\* Each State becomes a value in the state variable's range.
StateValues == {"invoked", "rendered", "refused"}

VARIABLES vpc   \* the state variable (program counter)

vars == <<vpc>>

TypeOK == vpc \in StateValues

\* Initial state: first listed in the spec (the format has no explicit initial marker).
Init == vpc = "invoked"

Next ==
  \* render_ok: invoked -> rendered (guard: [[render.contract.rc_stamp]])
  \/ vpc = "invoked" /\ vpc' = "rendered"
  \* refuse_format: invoked -> refused (guard: [[render.contract.rc_closed_formats]])
  \/ vpc = "invoked" /\ vpc' = "refused"
  \* refuse_input: invoked -> refused (guard: [[render.contract.rc_input_present]])
  \/ vpc = "invoked" /\ vpc' = "refused"
  \* refuse_write: rendered -> refused (guard: [[render.contract.rc_atomic_write]])
  \/ vpc = "rendered" /\ vpc' = "refused"
  \* stuttering: guards are prose (uninterpreted) — a terminal
  \* state must not read as an engine-side deadlock
  \/ UNCHANGED vpc

\* No state carries an `emits` field — Output is simply empty.
Output == << >>

